# Not uploaded to the edge. Keeps the UAT deployment to what a reader loads.
#
# .wrangler FIRST. Wrangler writes its own working files there during the
# deploy itself — including .wrangler/cache/wrangler-account.json, which holds
# the Cloudflare account id and name. It leaked to a public URL on the first
# deploy of both projects because this list did not name it.
.wrangler

.git
.gitignore
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.prod.jsonc
.claude
tools
worker
RELEASE.md
# The audit record. Generated into the repo root, which IS the assets directory,
# so without these two lines the next deploy would publish the company's entire
# release history — every version, every commit subject, question counts over
# time — at qpio.app/RELEASES.md. It reaches the CEO through hq.qpioapp.com,
# behind Cloudflare Access, and must not have a second public door.
RELEASES.md
releases.json
README.md
MORNING.md
RESEARCH.md
node_modules

# LOCAL TOOLING AND WORKING NOTES (29 Sep 2026). Found publicly downloadable on
# both qpio.app and uat.qpio.app: ruvector.db and .swarm/memory.db (agent-tool
# memory databases from July, no secrets inside), CLAUDE.md (agent
# instructions), scratchpad/ (commit notes), docs/ and a release note. None is
# part of the app. The rule this list now follows: the edge gets what a reader
# loads, and the check in tools/preflight.js fails the release if anything
# outside that list would be uploaded.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.swarm
.claude-flow
.ai
.github
.nojekyll
scripts
scratchpad
docs
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
PROJECT_STATUS.md
RELEASE-NOTE-*.md
package.json
package-lock.json
